<projects_info>
<project name="react-devtool" kind="react-library" open_source="true">
<description>Easy solution to have your own internal devtool, unleash the DX of React</description>

<features>
- A main view to lets user configure their app.
- A static button that live in your app, that when clicked, opens the devtool.
</features>

<structure>
- devtool.tsx that entrypoint of the library
- app.tsx that for Playground of the app
- /devtools, the legacy code copied from React Scan. The main logic is in this folder.
The flow is we will build devtool.tsx to publish on npm, and the user can import it in their app.
Devtool should be framework agnostic, and should be able to work with any framework, but start with React and Preact.
</structure>

<usage_guidelines>
in user's app, they can do:
```tsx
import { Devtool } from "react-devtool";

function App() {
  return (
    ...
      <Devtool plugins={[posthogPlugin, tanstackRouterPlugin]}>
      <UI
        featureFlagsSchema={featureFlagsSchema}
      />
      ... addtional ui as user needs
      <input type="text" />
      <button>Save</button>
      <Tabs>
        <Tab label="feature A">
          123
        </Tab>
      </Tabs>
    </Devtool>
    ...
  )
}
```
to import the devtool
</usage_guidelines>

<planned_features>
- Plugin system.
- Vite plugin that enables server side features.
</planned_features>

</project>
</projects_info>
